      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There isn't a single, universal consensus, but the modern trend among experts is toward affirming an open, non-judgmental environment. Choosing to *not* discuss it isn't inherently a failure, but actively avoiding acknowledging questions can sometimes send a message that the topic is taboo. The better approach is likely to tailor the conversation to your family's comfort level while prioritizing acceptance and listening to her questions as they arise.",
